      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] **Test Oracle Integrity \u0026 Anti-Masking Audit:** This assertion only verifies that the decryption operation returns success, but it does not verify that the unwrapped pairing key actually matches the originally computed shared secret. Please assert the exact expected bytes to prevent silent data corruption. \n\nAdditionally, there are no tests verifying the successful path for `FpP256Key::from_uncompressed_point` or `FpP256Key::from_private_key`—only their failure modes.\n\nSuggestion for verifying the unwrapped secret and happy paths:\n```cpp\n\tconst auto expected_secret \u003d key1-\u003ecompute_shared_secret(*key2);\n\tzassert_true(expected_secret.has_value());\n\n\tFpPairingKey::Bytes unwrapped{};\n\tzassert_true(\n\t\tFpPairingKey::unwrap_into(*wrapped, unwrapped).has_value());\n\tzassert_mem_equal(unwrapped.data(), expected_secret-\u003edata(),\n\t\t\t  unwrapped.size());\n\n\t// Test happy path for from_uncompressed_point\n\tstd::array\u003cuint8_t, FP_ASCP_KEY_SIZE\u003e valid_point{};\n\tvalid_point[0] \u003d POINT_CONVERSION_UNCOMPRESSED;\n\tstd::ranges::copy(pub2-\u003ex, valid_point.begin() + 1);\n\tstd::ranges::copy(pub2-\u003ey, valid_point.begin() + 1 + sizeof(pub2-\u003ex));\n\tzassert_true(FpP256Key::from_uncompressed_point(valid_point).has_value());\n\n\t// Test happy path for from_private_key\n\tstd::array\u003cuint8_t, FP_ELLIPTIC_CURVE_PRIVATE_KEY_LEN\u003e valid_priv{};\n\tvalid_priv[31] \u003d 1; // A valid simple scalar\n\tzassert_true(FpP256Key::from_private_key(valid_priv).has_value());\n```\n*(Also consider a minor safety improvement for the other `zassert_equal(..., EC_ERROR_INVAL)` assertions: calling `.error()` on an `std::expected` that accidentally succeeds invokes undefined behavior or crashes the test runner. Checking `!res.has_value()` first is safer.)* [🔗](http://go/tj/7b66bda6-c1b7-4de9-89f6-07c0434458a1)",
